# MANAK — Legal Metrology E-Commerce Compliance Checklist

**File:** `MANAK_Legal_Metrology_Checklist.md`  
**Scope:** Amazon / Flipkart / other Indian e-commerce product listings  
**Primary basis:** Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011, relevant amendments, and Department of Consumer Affairs e-commerce guidance.  
**Purpose:** Convert Legal Metrology requirements into an online-listing compliance rules engine.

> **Important:** This checklist is an e-commerce screening tool, not a legal certification. A marketplace page cannot establish every physical-package requirement. MANAK should distinguish **PASS**, **FAIL**, **CANNOT_CHECK**, **NOT_APPLICABLE**, and **VERIFY**.

---

## 1. Status model

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `PASS` | Required online information is present and passes the automated rule |
| `FAIL` | Required online information is absent or clearly inconsistent |
| `CANNOT_CHECK` | The rule requires physical inspection, measurement, sampling, or records not available from the page |
| `NOT_APPLICABLE` | Rule does not apply to this product/category |
| `VERIFY` | Listing provides an indicator, but a definitive legal conclusion needs external/physical evidence |

### Evidence levels

| Level | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `TEXT` | Can be checked from structured/listing text |
| `IMAGE` | Can be screened from product/package images |
| `CALCULATED` | Can be mathematically validated from listing data |
| `EXTERNAL` | Requires government/registration/database verification |
| `PHYSICAL` | Requires physical package/sample inspection |

