# 2. E-commerce-specific master rule

## ECOM-01 — Mandatory declarations on e-commerce website

**Legal basis:** Rule 6(10) / Department of Consumer Affairs FAQ.

An e-commerce entity must ensure that mandatory declarations specified under Rule 6(1), **except the month and year in which the commodity was manufactured or packed**, are displayed on the digital/electronic network used for e-commerce transactions.

**MANAK check:** `PASS / FAIL / VERIFY`

**Evidence:** `TEXT + IMAGE`

**Important implementation rule:**

```text
Do NOT mark an Amazon/Flipkart listing FAIL merely because
month/year of manufacture or packing is not displayed online.
```

