## 35. Source notes

The uploaded **Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011** document provides the core Rule 6 declarations, quantity rules, display-panel requirements, exemptions, registration provisions and advertisement provisions.

Current/official amendment material should be used alongside the older uploaded PDF. In particular:

- 2017 amendment introduced the e-commerce definitions and amended the packaged-commodity framework. 
- 2021 amendment introduced Rule 6(11) unit-sale-price declarations. 
- DCA FAQ explains the e-commerce unit-sale-price requirement and rounding. 
- 2022 garment amendment created the Rule 26(f) garment/hosiery provisions and expressly required the relevant information to be displayed on an e-commerce website. 
- 2023 amendment changed the commencement date of a 2022 amendment to 1 October 2023. 

**Official sources:**

- Department of Consumer Affairs — Legal Metrology notifications
- Legal Metrology (Packaged Commodities) Rules, 2011
- Department of Consumer Affairs — Legal Metrology FAQ

